In order to explain non-linear  optical phenomena  of biological  systems, it is
importan t to remember the general but at the same time basic property of all
biological  tissues of representing opticall y “dense ” matter. This means that the
intermole cular distances are small compared with the waveleng th of the light .
Under these condition s the theory of Dicke (195 4) has to be applied in order to
understand the interact ion of light and matter. According to Dicke, sponta -
neous reemission of absorbed light is impossib le as soon as the intermole cular
