ence of light waves cumulating up to coherent light flashes which are then
emitted in relatively  short time intervals . Sub-radia nce is defined as the de-
structive interferenc e of the light waves within the system of absorbing mole -
cules. The result is “delayed luminesce nce” of coherent light waves whic h
relax according to hyperbolic functions.  Just this situatio n is displayed in bio-
logical systems. Consequen tly, the explanati on of the results on normal and
tumor cells follows the general theory of Dicke .
